<Layout title="Privacy Policy">
	<main class='container'>
		<h1>Privacy Policy (Datenschutzerklärung)</h1>

		<h2>1. General Information and Data Controller</h2>
		<p>
			The following privacy policy provides an overview of what happens to your personal data when you visit this website. Personal data comprises all data that can be used to identify you personally.
		</p>
		<p>
			The data controller responsible for data processing on this website within the meaning of the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) is:
		</p>
		<p>
			Lukas Horn<br />
			Sanderglacisstraße 6a<br />
			97072 Würzburg<br />
			Germany<br />
			Email: research@lukas-horn.de
		</p>

		<h2>2. Hosting on GitHub Pages</h2>
		<p>
			This website is hosted by GitHub Pages, a service provided by GitHub Inc., 88 Colin P. Kelly Jr. Street, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA.
		</p>
		<p>
			When you visit this website, your browser automatically transfers certain information to GitHub's servers to deliver the website content. This information includes your IP address, browser type and version, operating system, referrer URL, and the time of your request. This data is processed to ensure the secure and reliable operation of the website.
		</p>
		<p>
			The legal basis for this processing is our legitimate interest in providing a secure and functioning website in accordance with Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. For further details on how GitHub handles your data, please refer to the <a href='https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'>GitHub Privacy Statement</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>3. Cookies and Analytics</h2>
		<p>
			This static website does not directly utilise cookies or web tracking analytics (such as Google Analytics) to track visitor behaviour. If you follow external links to other platforms, their respective privacy policies apply.
		</p>

		<h2>4. Google OAuth and Google Drive Access</h2>
		<p>
			This website also serves as the privacy policy for a Google Cloud OAuth 2.0 client that is used to access Google Drive, for example from desktop or command-line applications. Any user may authorize this client to access their own Google Drive account; access is strictly limited to the account that grants it. The operator of this website does not receive, view, or store any data accessed through this client.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Data accessed:</strong> Google Drive file metadata and file contents of the Google account that authorizes the client.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Purpose and use:</strong> The data is used solely so that the authorizing user can access, back up, synchronize, or manage their own Google Drive. It is not used for advertising or profiling, and it is not shared with, sold to, or transferred to any third party.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Storage:</strong> Google OAuth access and refresh tokens are stored locally on the authorizing user's own device. They are never transmitted to or stored on this website. This website has no login and does not itself process any Google user data.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Google API Services User Data Policy:</strong> The use of information received from Google APIs adheres to the <a href='https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'>Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Revoking access:</strong> Authorization can be revoked at any time on the <a href='https://myaccount.google.com/permissions' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'>Google Account permissions page</a>, after which the locally stored tokens become invalid.
		</p>

		<h2>5. Your Rights</h2>
		<p>
			Under the GDPR, you have the right to request information about the origin, recipient, and purpose of your stored personal data at any time, free of charge. You also have the right to request that this data be corrected, blocked, or deleted. Furthermore, you can object to the processing of your data and request data portability.
		</p>
		<p>
			To exercise these rights, or if you have any questions regarding privacy and data protection, you may contact the data controller at any time. Additionally, you have the right to lodge a complaint with the competent supervisory authority (e.g., the Bavarian State Office for Data Protection Supervision).
		</p>
	</main>
</Layout>
